===== min_heap_ops 280
158 | A heap is a row of numbers in positions LIST, ... where the number in position p is never larger than the numbers in positions Np and Np+N (when those exist). To add a number: put it in the first free position at the end, then, while it is smaller than the number in position (its position divided by N, rounded down), swap the two. To remove the smallest: take out the number in position N, put the number from the last position into position N (the row is now one shorter), then, while it is larger than the smaller of the numbers in positions Np and Np+N (those that exist), swap it with that smaller number. Start with an empty heap and add these numbers in order: LIST. Give the row from position N to the end, separated by commas.
80 | A heap is a row of numbers in positions LIST, ... where the number in position p is never larger than the numbers in positions Np and Np+N (when those exist). To add a number: put it in the first free position at the end, then, while it is smaller than the number in position (its position divided by N, rounded down), swap the two. To remove the smallest: take out the number in position N, put the number from the last position into position N (the row is now one shorter), then, while it is larger than the smaller of the numbers in positions Np and Np+N (those that exist), swap it with that smaller number. Start with an empty heap and add these numbers in order: LIST. Then remove the smallest N time. Give the row from position N to the end, separated by commas.
42 | A heap is a row of numbers in positions LIST, ... where the number in position p is never larger than the numbers in positions Np and Np+N (when those exist). To add a number: put it in the first free position at the end, then, while it is smaller than the number in position (its position divided by N, rounded down), swap the two. To remove the smallest: take out the number in position N, put the number from the last position into position N (the row is now one shorter), then, while it is larger than the smaller of the numbers in positions Np and Np+N (those that exist), swap it with that smaller number. Start with an empty heap and add these numbers in order: LIST. Then remove the smallest N times. Give the row from position N to the end, separated by commas.
keys {('removals', 'xs'): 280}
extra {1: 80, 0: 158, 2: 42}
